problem_statement:
Metadata V16: Add version number to Runtime API trait information
It would be useful in some cases to expose the version of each Runtime API that a runtime supports in the metadata.

ie we should take this struct https://github.com/paritytech/frame-metadata/blob/0fc0539c2def93b5ca2d71deb5fa1c9d87c9b7c3/frame-metadata/src/v16.rs#L94:

```rust
pub struct RuntimeApiMetadata<T: Form = MetaForm> {
	/// Trait name.
	pub name: T::String,
	/// Trait methods.
	pub methods: Vec<RuntimeApiMethodMetadata<T>>,
	/// Trait documentation.
	pub docs: Vec<T::String>,
	/// Deprecation info
	pub deprecation_info: DeprecationStatus<T>,
}
```

And add something like `pub version: Compact<u32>` which would be the version of a given Runtime API trait that is being implemented.

Knowing this version can help callers understand which runtime calls they will need to make to obtain some data.

### Alternative Approach

The `System.version` constant also contains this information against hashes of the Runtime API trait names. Constants are already added to the Metadata, so we could use this instead, though it is less accessible/usable/obvious than the suggested addition.

