problem_statement:
Century cutoff for %y undocumented
If I run
```rust
use chrono::NaiveDate;


fn main() {
    let res = NaiveDate::parse_from_str("01-01-69", "%d-%m-%y");
    println!("res: {:?}", res);
    let res = NaiveDate::parse_from_str("01-01-70", "%d-%m-%y");
    println!("res: {:?}", res);
}
```
I get
```
res: Ok(2069-01-01)
res: Ok(1970-01-01)
```

It seems that 70 is the cutoff, but the docs don't mention it https://docs.rs/chrono/latest/chrono/format/strftime/index.html#fn1

